refix. Scan with `i`; whenever `nums[i]` is non-zero, swap it into position `insert` and advance `insert`. Everything before `insert` is non-zero and in original order; everything between `insert` and `i` is zero.\n\n**Why it works:** the invariant `nums[insert..i-1]` are all zeros holds because a non-zero at `i` is always swapped out of that range immediately, so the swap only ever exchanges a non-zero with a zero (or with itself).\n\n**Common mistakes:** a two-pass overwrite-then-fill version is fine but interviewers often ask for a single pass; using `nums.remove(0)` in a loop (O(n^2) and shifts the array); losing stability of the non-zero order by swapping from the back.\n\n**Interview follow-ups:** Minimise the number of writes (only swap when `i != insert`). Move a different value, or all elements satisfying a predicate, to the end (same partition). Partition into three groups in one pass (Dutch National Flag, see Sort Colors).","complexity":{"time":"O(n)","space":"O(1)"},"similar":["remove-duplicates-from-sorted-array","sort-colors","remove-element"],"number":15,"starter":"class Solution:\n    def moveZeroes(self, nums: List[int]) -> None:\n        pass\n"}